## Methodology note on the cold reads

Two of the cold reads behind this notice returned findings that were adopted only
in part, and the record names what was rejected.

**CT-S13-COLDREAD5** returned **ERROR** on a sufficiency inference in C4 and
located the strong-Riemann-Hilbert restriction now quoted at point 5. Both were
adopted, and the claim text was weakened accordingly.

**CT-S14-COLDREAD-B** established the normal-form identity now stated under the
C4 table. Its description of the integer-difference points as *apparent* was
**rejected**: by the lemma of **C1**, residue 1 with Q at most a simple pole
forces a log term, so those points are non-apparent. Its substantive conclusion,
that they are not ordinary, was adopted. That reader was isolated from **C1** by
design and could not have known.

**CT-S15-COLDREAD-DEFERRED** was supplied with page images and ran **OCR** on
them. Two of its transcriptions were **rejected** after the pages were re-read
directly: it rendered the constant matrix in Jimbo's (3.1) as (1/2)sigma_3
where the page prints diag(1,0), and it reported (A1)_PV as constraining
theta_inf as well as theta_0 and theta_t, where the page prints only
theta_0, theta_t not in Z. Neither error reached this notice; the (A1) line
and the PV dictionary quoted in **C2** were verified earlier by direct reading and
are correct as printed. Its two verdicts, and the p. 2635 M(t) sentence it
located, were adopted.

None of this is machine-checked, and the notice must not claim otherwise.

## Deposit-day checklist (P0 citation rule) — NOT YET DONE, and deliberately so

The operator's ruling: perform this pass **immediately before uploading**, not
now, so that the recorded hashes match what is actually cited on the day.

| # | External citation | Action on deposit day |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | van der Put & Saito, *Ann. Inst. Fourier* **59** (2009), Table 2.1, p. 2635, and the strong-Riemann–Hilbert passage on p. 2634 | re-fetch, record sha256, re-read **both** page images |
| 2 | Jimbo, *Publ. RIMS*, p. 1152 — the PV dictionary **and** assumption (A1)_PV | re-fetch, record sha256, re-read the page image |
| 3 | Companion v1.2 (Zenodo version DOI) — Remark 2.2, Conjecture 4.1, the tuple, the scaling paragraph on p. 6, §7.1 | re-fetch from Zenodo, record sha256, confirm it is still the version cited |
| 4 | DLMF §32.2 (cited by v1.2 for the PV normalisation) | re-fetch, record the **release version and date**, not just the URL |

Per the rule, **hypotheses as well as theorem statements** are in scope — that
is the lesson of the Gautschi (2.8) near-miss, where an OCR layer rendered the
hypothesis in a way that would have reversed the conclusion. Read page images,
never the text layer, for anything load-bearing.

